	"department": "ENGL",
	"description": [
		"This course introduces students to the comparative study of Afro-Caribbean literature. Students explore the literature of the region after the 1950s in a relational framework to understand the commonalities and differences of its peoples, cultures, and literatures. Students read novels, essays, theory, and poetry from different linguistic and cultural areas of the region. Specific attention will be given to the genre of marvelous realism. Offered periodically in spring semester. Prerequisite: WRIT 120 or equivalent."
	],
